Use case: identity-preserve. Asset type: a TWELVE-frame sprite animation sheet for a Godot obstacle enemy.
Reference image 1 is the EXACT monster identity to preserve (cap outline, five cap spots, four upper and four lower teeth, pale blue stalk, two short arms, two root feet, eye shape). Reference image 2 is the desired VERY FLAT matte colored-outline rendering.
Create exactly 12 full-body copies of the SAME bite-cap monster in 12 successive poses of ONE seamless grounded breathing/chomp loop. This is not twelve different character designs. Preserve cap spot positions and proportions in every frame. Simplify the reference rendering to large SOLID FLAT FILLS with at most one solid shadow plane, NO gradients, no shine, no glossy tooth facets. Medium muted plum colored outline, NO black contour. Dusty rose cap, pale blue stalk, muted mauve mouth and cool ivory teeth. Clean 2D hand-drawn storybook style.
Layout is mandatory: exactly THREE COLUMNS and FOUR ROWS in a uniform invisible rectangular grid, read left-to-right then top-to-bottom. Target canvas 1536x2048. Each cell has precisely ONE complete monster, centered on its own column, feet on the same relative baseline at 90% of each cell height. Equal object scale across all 12 cells. Keep wide transparent gutters and at least 10% padding inside each cell. No cell borders or labels, no numbers, no scene, no shadow, grass, particles or extra objects. Entire background and gutters genuinely transparent.
Pose sequence, frames 1 through 12:
1 neutral medium-open cap jaw, arms down;
2 jaw begins closing, stalk slightly taller;
3 jaw nearly closed, arms curl inward;
4 jaw fully closed, stalk anticipatory squat;
5 jaw starts opening, arms begin lifting;
6 jaw opens broadly, stalk stretches;
7 jaw at widest single chomp, arms raised slightly;
8 jaw remains broad, stalk soft squash;
9 jaw closing toward medium, arms lowering;
10 medium-open jaw, stalk recovers;
11 relaxed medium jaw, arms almost down;
12 pose almost identical to frame 1, halfway approaching its exact neutral height, for a smooth loop back to frame 1.
Only small controlled 5-10% motion; two feet remain planted at fixed baseline and character remains frontal. Teeth remain attached to the jaws, anatomy never changes. All TWELVE frames must be visibly present and cleanly separable. Transparent RGBA.

Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: one 12-frame animation sprite sheet for a Godot mobile runner obstacle.
Reference image 1 is the earlier mushroom scene palette and hand-drawn fantasy gill shapes, use as style reference only. Reference image 2 is the newly generated bite-cap animation sheet, copy its restrained matte colored-outline game-art style, NOT its identity. Reference images 3 and 4 are character design inspiration only, do not copy pixel art or bright colors.
Create ONE distinct original poison mushroom enemy: A low rounded bell-cap poisonous mushroom monster. Muted teal cap with exactly five large flat dusty-rose toxin spots, a scalloped rim, and three soft drooping gill fringes. Beneath is a small pale mint squat stalk face with two narrow angled eyes and two little blunt fangs. Two soft curved flipper arms and two tiny root feet. Wide low silhouette, mischievous threatening look, no props.
Palette: desaturated petrol teal #719F9E, dusty rose spots #BC8198, pale mint #CAD9CB; medium gray teal #5F8181 outlines. Clean FLAT matte hand-drawn illustration, solid broad fills and maximum one flat shadow shape. Colored medium gray teal outlines, no black contour, no gloss, no lighting gradients, no grain, texture, noise, particles or mist.
Create TWELVE sequential full-body poses of the SAME bell-cap monster for a gentle grounded looping motion: A grounded gentle side-to-side sway and breathing cycle: bell rim and three fringes sway left and right with delayed follow-through, two flipper arms alternately lift a little, face stays frontal and eyes keep their hostile squint. Feet planted.
Layout mandatory: exactly THREE COLUMNS and FOUR ROWS, uniform invisible grid, chronological order left-to-right then top-to-bottom. Target 1536x2048 genuine transparent RGBA. Precisely one entire monster per cell, at equal scale, same relative center and same planted root-feet baseline at 90% cell height. Leave transparent padding and clear gutters. No labels, numbers, grid lines, decorative foliage, poison clouds, floor shadows or extra objects.
Sequence 1-12:
1 neutral cap and arms;
2 cap leans 2 degrees left, right flipper begins lifting;
3 cap leans 4 degrees left, fringes follow;
4 cap leans 5 degrees left, right flipper highest;
5 lean eases to 3 degrees left;
6 return nearly neutral, right flipper lowers;
7 neutral passing toward right;
8 cap leans 2 degrees right, left flipper begins lifting;
9 cap leans 4 degrees right, fringes follow;
10 cap leans 5 degrees right, left flipper highest;
11 ease to 2 degrees right, arms relax;
12 almost neutral matching the start.
Tiny gentle breathing only, not walking or hopping. Exactly five toxin spots stay fixed on the teal cap, exactly three fringes, two narrow eyes, two small mouth fangs, two flipper arms, two root feet in every frame. The face always looks toward the approaching player. Distinct low broad bell silhouette, clear complete cutouts.

Use case: identity-preserve. Asset type: 12-frame FRONT-FACING RUNNING sprite sheet for a Godot runner enemy.
Image 1 is the EXACT three-eye morel mushroom identity from its existing idle sheet. Preserve the same tapered mauve cone cap, honeycomb cavity markings and EXACTLY three cream eyes (one high central and two lower), pale lavender squat stalk, tiny three-tooth grin, two short arms and two root feet. Image 2 supplies a running mushroom pose reference only; do NOT copy its large cap jaw or rose identity.
Create twelve NEW poses of this three-eye monster RUNNING TOWARDS THE VIEWER, frontal camera, in place. Forward movement happens in Godot. Same scale and same identity in every pose. Running must be clear, knees lifting with feet alternately thrust towards camera and opposite arms pumping, small body compression and airborne phase. Retain threatening face; three cap eyes blink subtly during the same run.
Mandatory layout: exactly THREE columns and FOUR rows in an invisible equal grid, 12 complete separate sprites, chronological row-major order. Target 1536x2048 genuine alpha background. Keep a generous 12% transparent safety margin in EACH cell, especially below feet. Do not crop any root toe or pointed cap. No captions, numbers, grids, ground shadow, floor, foliage, dust, particles or scenery.
LOCK LEG PHASES rather than randomly swapping raised foot:
1 anatomical LEFT foot planted forward (viewer RIGHT), RIGHT leg lifted behind (viewer LEFT), RIGHT arm forward;
2 same LEFT support leg compresses, RIGHT leg begins forward swing;
3 RIGHT knee and foot (viewer LEFT) are raised forward, LEFT support foot behind;
4 both feet airborne, RIGHT foot/viewer LEFT reaching ahead, LEFT foot trailing;
5 RIGHT foot/viewer LEFT dropping toward contact;
6 RIGHT foot/viewer LEFT plants, LEFT foot/viewer RIGHT starts lift behind;
7 RIGHT foot/viewer LEFT supports, LEFT foot/viewer RIGHT swings forward, LEFT arm forward;
8 RIGHT support compresses as LEFT knee lifts;
9 LEFT knee/viewer RIGHT passes high forward;
10 airborne, LEFT foot/viewer RIGHT reaches ahead, RIGHT trails;
11 LEFT foot/viewer RIGHT lowers toward ground;
12 LEFT foot/viewer RIGHT nearly plants, RIGHT foot lifts behind, approaching the exact pose 1.
Do not change which foot is forward at random. Keep three eye locations, cavity layout, cap size, tooth count and limb count consistent. Flat matte hand-drawn style, broad solid desaturated mauve and lavender fills and a single shadow plane; colored medium plum outlines, no black contour, glossy highlights, oily gradients, excess texture or grain. Seamless loop.

